# unit-tests.list: kvm-unit-tests' tests in the KVM suite, one a line: the
# test's name in x86/unittests.cfg, what corpus.sh requires of it under
# Rach2's KVM, Linux's result on the testing PC, and the reason. EXPECT is
# `pass`; `skip`, the test's own skip for what the processor or QEMU lacks,
# as Linux skips it there, with its reason; or `excluded`, not run, for one
# of the reasons the stack's approved plan allows. LINUX is the result of
# Linux 6.18.58, WSL's, with QEMU 10.2.1 and kernel-irqchip=split, as
# ref/linux-unit-tests.txt has it: a row Linux failed
# there still expects a pass, its failure named after `Linux:`.
#
# NAME EXPECT LINUX REASON
access pass pass
access-reduced-maxphyaddr skip skip /sys/module/kvm_intel/parameters/allow_smaller_maxphyaddr not equal to Y
access_fep skip skip Forced emulation prefix (FEP) not available
asyncpf pass pass
cet skip skip No CET features supported
cmpxchg8b excluded skip i386: built only for i386, and the staged tests are x86-64's
debug pass fail Linux: unhandled #PF at ffff0ff0 and 404fb8
emulator pass pass
ept excluded skip nested virtualization, excluded by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10: Rach2's KVM gives its guests neither SVM nor VMX
ept-mbec excluded skip nested virtualization, excluded by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10: Rach2's KVM gives its guests neither SVM nor VMX
eventinj pass pass
hypercall pass pass
hyperv_clock excluded pass Hyper-V: Rach2's KVM has no Hyper-V enlightenments
hyperv_connections excluded fail Hyper-V: Rach2's KVM has no Hyper-V enlightenments
hyperv_stimer excluded pass Hyper-V: Rach2's KVM has no Hyper-V enlightenments
hyperv_stimer_direct excluded pass Hyper-V: Rach2's KVM has no Hyper-V enlightenments
hyperv_synic excluded pass Hyper-V: Rach2's KVM has no Hyper-V enlightenments
idt_test pass pass
intel_iommu pass pass
ioapic pass pass
kvmclock_test pass pass
la57 pass fail Linux: la57.c:230: assert failed: write_cr4_safe(read_cr4() | X86_CR4_PCIDE) == 0
lam pass pass
memory pass pass
msr pass pass
msr64 pass pass
pcid-asymmetric pass pass
pcid-disabled pass fail Linux: FAIL: Test on INVPCID when disabled
pcid-enabled pass pass
pks skip skip PKS not enabled: the processor has no PKS
pku skip skip PKU not enabled
pmu excluded fail PMU: Rach2's KVM gives its guests no performance counters
pmu_lbr excluded skip PMU: Rach2's KVM gives its guests no performance counters
pmu_pebs excluded skip PMU: Rach2's KVM gives its guests no performance counters
rdpru pass pass
realmode pass pass
rmap_chain pass pass
s3 pass pass
